{"name":"Ritzy","hex":"#d79c5f","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"ritzy","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Elegant and luxurious."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/ritzy"}],"entries":[{"title":"Ritzy","blocks":[{"text":"Ritzy is a lost 1927 American comedy silent film directed by Richard Rosson and written by Elinor Glyn, Percy Heath, Robert N. Lee and George Marion Jr. The film stars Betty Bronson, James Hall, William Austin, Joan Standing, George Nichols and Roscoe Karns. The film was released on April 9, 1927, by Paramount Pictures."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/ed/Ritzy_%281927%29_Poster.jpg/330px-Ritzy_%281927%29_Poster.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ritzy","wikidata":"Q19321773"},{"title":"Ritzy (play)","blocks":[{"text":"Ritzy is a 1930 comedy play by Sidney Toler and Viva Tattersall. It ran for 32 performances at the Longacre Theatre on Broadway with a cast that included Miriam Hopkins and Ernest Truex. A financially struggling couple living in a cheap hotel believe they have inherited a huge sum of money, until the discovery of closer relatives means they will not receive the fortune."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ritzy_(play)","wikidata":"Q96402047"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/7a/Ritzy_1927_Lobby_Card_01.jpg/120px-Ritzy_1927_Lobby_Card_01.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/7a/Ritzy_1927_Lobby_Card_01.jpg/250px-Ritzy_1927_Lobby_Card_01.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/7a/Ritzy_1927_Lobby_Card_01.jpg/120px-Ritzy_1927_Lobby_Card_01.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.